Factory Droid SDK for Haskell

This port is derived from the Factory Droid SDK public contracts and schemas.
The reference Python and TypeScript SDKs are distributed under Apache-2.0.

Upstream notice retained from the Python SDK:
Copyright 2025 The San Francisco AI Factory, Inc

The supplied JSON Schema documents are reproduced unchanged. Their provenance
and fingerprints are recorded in schema/manifest.json and docs/parity.md.

Hosted MCP transport contracts were also inspected in @modelcontextprotocol/sdk
1.29.0, distributed under the MIT license. No JavaScript runtime is required.

Hosted schema validation uses the separately built native factory-droid-validator
worker, based on jsonschema 0.55.1 (MIT), with serde_json preserving exact values.
Its resolved dependency license and notice texts are included in
native/schema-validator/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt and embedded in the worker's
--licenses output. The source package and lockfile are shipped with this SDK.
The worker-local jsonschema source modification and its archive provenance are
documented in native/schema-validator/VENDOR.md; the original MIT notice is retained.

The former Haskell jsonschema-0.3.0.1 dependency (DPella AB) has been removed.
Its MPL metadata versus LicenseRef-AllRightsReserved source-header discrepancy
is retained as historical evidence, not a license grant used by this release.
